    "long_instructions": "# Cleaning Data\r\n\r\n#### In this warm-up activity, students will write what they notice and what they wonder about the visualization.  \r\n\r\n#### Look at two graphs trying to help someone answer the question: “When should we have the party?”\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/7e010252c79b9ea18ad1709c47913cde-image-1721314333157.png\" alt=\"spreadsheet of dataset with pizza preferences\" alt=\"diagram of software: system software, application software, and utlity software with examples of icons of each\" alt=\"chatbot lab level\" width=\"80%\" style=\"border: 2px solid black; border-radius: 8px; display: block; margin: auto\">\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/376f6fc4810525fd42748cf7661b5f71-image-1721314350825.png\" alt=\"spreadsheet of dataset with pizza preferences\" alt=\"diagram of software: system software, application software, and utlity software with examples of icons of each\" alt=\"chatbot lab level\" width=\"80%\" style=\"border: 2px solid black; border-radius: 8px; display: block; margin: auto;\">\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n#### In the reflection box below answer the following questions:\r\n- #### *What do you notice? What do you wonder?*\r\n- #### *Which of these makes it easier for a human to decide when the party should be? Explain your answer.*\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #a6e3e8; border-radius: 40px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 1px 20px 1px 20px;\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 18px; \"><strong>Teacher Tip:</strong> After students have had a chance to write a couple things they noticed and wondered, instruct students to share with their partner. Give students a few minutes to share before bringing the class back together for a <b>data talk</b>. \r\n</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n",
